  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "Jxs3BFdGOvBUzmofUOt1HkauN/A=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:37.908Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Groupe Onepoint is recorded at over EUR 500m turnover, operating from Paris and seven further cities, dual-certified with Camunda Silver alongside its Flowable listing. It is the largest French presence in the Flowable sweep and, at that turnover, an enterprise-scale sale.\n\nThe dual position is the substantive part. Camunda and Flowable are the same architectural gap twice: both orchestrate when things happen while holding the process or case instance as mutable state with purgeable history, so neither owns the append-only, user-attributed record of what was decided. A partner certified on both can reuse one integration across two platforms, which improves the economics of the first build for whoever does it.\n\nThe row also carries a data-quality flag \u2014 no website link on the Flowable card. Forty2's card in the same sweep has the identical omission, so this looks like patchy directory data rather than anything about the firms; either way the domain needs confirming before outreach. Provenance: Flowable Partner Finder (flowable.com/company/partners), mined 2026-08-18, not imprint-swept.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- Groupe Onepoint (FR Paris + 7 cities) \u2014 groupeonepoint.com\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> EUR 500M+ turnover. DUAL: Camunda Silver. No website link on the Flowable card \u00b7 SOURCE: Flowable Partner Finder (flowable.com/company/partners), mined 2026-08-18. NOT imprint-swept.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:32:37.908534Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:37.908538Z"
    }
  },
